{"chunk_id": "c2c61e11789a", "text": "Kesini returns to Damayanti and recounts astonishing signs that the mysterious charioteer Vahuka possesses supernatural mastery: doors rise for him, vessels fill with water at a glance, fire springs from grass, flames cannot burn him, and crushed flowers become more fragrant. Damayanti, increasingly certain that Vahuka is her lost husband Nala in disguise, tests him further by tasting food he has cooked\u2014recognizing his skill immediately. She sends their children to him, and Nala, unable to hide his emotions, embraces them and weeps before withdrawing to avoid suspicion. With her doubts nearly resolved, Damayanti arranges to meet him directly. Confronting Vahuka, she laments Nala\u2019s abandonment in the forest. Nala reveals that the spirit Kali had possessed him and caused his actions, and that he has now overcome it, returning for her sake, though he fears she may have chosen another husband.\nKesini reports Vahuka\u2019s supernatural feats; Damayanti tests him, confirms he is Nala, and they confront their painful separation and suspicions.\nThemes: recognition of identity, marital fidelity, supernatural signs, separation and reunion, curse of Kali", "vector": [0.011450568214058876, -0.021266339346766472, 0.0016400371678173542, -0.018276197835803032, -0.02762388437986374, 0.021741408854722977, -0.03241649642586708, -0.013518516905605793, -0.008369604125618935, -0.01690687984228134, 0.023627713322639465, 0.0321090966463089, 0.0028539092745631933, 0.01525810919702053, -0.0004052061995025724, -0.003042539581656456, 0.04504775255918503, -0.020358119159936905, 0.019156472757458687, -0.025500046089291573, -0.00609206547960639, 0.0076989177614450455, 0.0012610296253114939, -0.004593501333147287, -0.03361814096570015, 0.013092352077364922, 0.023390179499983788, -0.014000573195517063, -0.0033866155426949263, -0.024857304990291595, 0.004775145556777716, -0.005498229060322046, 0.0010086490074172616, -0.01866742968559265, -0.03414910